      "exam_answer_md": "The **Rothschild Index** measures the elasticity of industry demand relative to that of an individual firm: **R = ET / EF**. It lies between 0 (perfect competition) and 1 (monopoly); with many firms producing similar products it is close to zero. **Application:** it measures the market power of firms in an industry, e.g. Tobacco and Chemicals 1.00, Food 0.26."
