      "memory_trick": "",
      "exam_answer_md": "The **Lerner Index** L = (P - MC) / P measures the difference between price and marginal cost as a fraction of price. It ranges from 0 to 1. When P = MC it is zero and the firm has no market power; closer to 1 indicates weak price competition and market power."
    },
    {
      "id": "be-s11-rothschild-lerner-c3",
      "heading": "From Lerner index to markup factor",
      "explanation_md": "Rearranging L = (P - MC) / P gives **P = [1 / (1 - L)] x MC**. The **markup factor** is **1/(1 - L)**.\n\n- L = 0: markup factor 1, so **P = MC**.\n- L = 0.20: markup factor **1/0.80 = 1.25**, so price is **1.25 times MC**.\n\nIn the slide's table, Tobacco has L = 0.76 and a markup factor of 4.17.",
      "example_ids": [
        "be-ex-lerner-table"
      ],
      "key_terms": [],
      "exam_line": "Markup factor = 1/(1-L); L = 0.20 gives 1.25.",
