    {
      "id": "be-s11-rothschild-lerner-q-8d6e24a4",
      "type": "short",
      "stem": "Explain the Rothschild index and the Lerner index.",
      "options": [],
      "answer": "",
      "accept": [],
      "explanation": "",
      "model_answer_md": "**Rothschild index:** R = ET / EF, the elasticity of total market demand over the elasticity of one firm's demand. It lies between **0 (perfect competition)** and **1 (monopoly)**; many firms with similar products push it toward zero.\n\n**Lerner index:** L = (P - MC) / P, the price-cost gap as a fraction of price, from 0 to 1. L = 0 when P = MC (no market power); closer to 1 means market power. It gives the **markup factor 1/(1-L)**: L = 0.20 means price is 1.25 times MC.",
      "rubric": [
        {
          "point": "Rothschild formula",
          "source_ref": "be--session-11#10"
        },
